## TLDR Problem this solves: - No way to define custom roles with scoped permissions - Built-in roles are all-or-nothing, so admins over-grant - Unknown roles silently fell back to internal_user How it solves it: - Proxy admins define named roles allow-listing routes - Roles come from config or new /custom_role endpoints - Roles inherit other roles, cycles resolve safely - Governed roles are default deny on every ungranted route ## User Flow Before: a proxy admin who wants a user that can only read key and team info has to hand them internal_user, which also lets them create keys 1. The admin sends POST https://litellm-domain/user/new with `{"user_id": "analyst", "user_role": "read-only-analyst"}` and gets 422 back, since only the four built-in role names are accepted 2. Settling for the built-in role, they send POST https://litellm-domain/user/new with `{"user_id": "analyst", "user_role": "internal_user"}` and get 200 3. The analyst's key calls POST https://litellm-domain/key/generate and gets 200, minting keys the admin never wanted them to have 4. Another user could be granted read-only intent but still create keys and spend budget After: the admin defines the role once and the analyst is limited to exactly the routes it names 1. The admin sends POST https://litellm-domain/custom_role/new with `{"role_name": "read-only-analyst", "allowed_routes": ["/key/info", "/team/info"]}` and gets 201 with the stored role 2. They send POST https://litellm-domain/user/new with `{"user_id": "analyst", "user_role": "read-only-analyst"}` and get 200 3. The analyst's key calls GET https://litellm-domain/key/info and gets 200 4. The same key calls POST https://litellm-domain/key/generate and gets 403 saying `user_role=read-only-analyst is not allowed to access route=/key/generate` 5. The admin sends GET https://litellm-domain/custom_role/list and sees config defined and DB defined roles side by side 6. Another user holding that role can read info routes and can no longer create keys or touch anything the role does not list ## Relevant issues ## Linear ticket ## Pre-Submission checklist - [x] I have added meaningful tests - [x] The handful of test files covering my change pass locally, e.g. `uv run pytest tests/test_litellm/<your_test_file>.py -v` - [x] My PR passes all required CI/CD checks (e.g., lint, schema.d.ts sync check, etc.) - [x] My PR's scope is as isolated as possible; it only solves 1 specific problem - [ ] I have received a Greptile **Confidence Score of at least 4/5** before requesting a maintainer review ## Screenshots / Proof of Fix Two proxies were run side by side against local Postgres so every case has a real Before and After: the merge base `a112ba5f63` (`origin/litellm_internal_staging`) in a separate worktree on port 4001 with its own database, and the branch tip `b7f594d868` on port 4000. Both use `litellm/proxy/dev_config.yaml` with `master_key: sk-1234` and real provider credentials from `.env`, so the LLM case is a live Anthropic call. ```bash # shared setup sudo service postgresql start (cd litellm/proxy && uv run --no-sync prisma db push --accept-data-loss --skip-generate) # After: branch tip on :4000 uv run --no-sync litellm --config litellm/proxy/dev_config.yaml --port 4000 # Before: merge base in its own worktree and database, on :4001 git worktree add /tmp/litellm_before a112ba5f63 createdb litellm_before (cd /tmp/litellm_before/litellm/proxy && DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/litellm_before \ prisma db push --accept-data-loss --skip-generate) PYTHONPATH=/tmp/litellm_before DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/litellm_before \ litellm --config /tmp/litellm_before/litellm/proxy/dev_config.yaml --port 4001 # the PYTHONPATH matters: without it the editable install resolves to the branch checkout, not the merge base ``` ### Before (a112ba5f63) #### Role CRUD 1. Create a role ```bash $ curl -s -X POST -H "Authorization: Bearer sk-1234" -H "Content-Type: application/j