HTTP:%{http_code}
" {"detail":"Not Found"} HTTP:404 ``` 4. Delete a role ```bash $ curl -s -X POST -H "Authorization: Bearer sk-1234" -H "Content-Type: application/json" \ http://localhost:4001/custom_role/delete -d '{"role_name":"read-only-analyst"}' -w "
HTTP:%{http_code}
" {"detail":"Not Found"} HTTP:404 ``` #### Invalid role input 1. Reserved built-in name, bogus permission, and unknown parent role all hit the same missing endpoint, so nothing is validated ```bash $ for body in '{"role_name":"internal_user","allowed_routes":["/key/info"]}' \ '{"role_name":"bad-perm-role","allowed_routes":["nonsense"]}' \ '{"role_name":"child-of-nothing","allowed_routes":["/key/info"],"inherits":["does-not-exist"]}'; do curl -s -X POST -H "Authorization: Bearer sk-1234" -H "Content-Type: application/json" \ http://localhost:4001/custom_role/new -d "$body" -w " HTTP:%{http_code}
"; done {"detail":"Not Found"} HTTP:404 {"detail":"Not Found"} HTTP:404 {"detail":"Not Found"} HTTP:404 ``` #### Assigning a custom role to a user 1. Any role name outside the four built-ins is rejected by the request schema ```bash $ curl -s -X POST -H "Authorization: Bearer sk-1234" -H "Content-Type: application/json" \ http://localhost:4001/user/new \ -d '{"user_id":"rbac-analyst","user_email":"rbac-analyst@test.com","user_role":"read-only-analyst"}' \ -w "
